{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2020-07-25 21:30:00', 'title': 'PG&E PROVIDES UPDATE ON EQUITY EXIT FINANCING OVER-ALLOTMENT OUTCOME', 'text': 'PROVIDES UPDATE ON EQUITY EXIT FINANCING OVER-ALLOTMENT OUTCOME.UNDERWRITERS OF PREVIOUSLY ANNOUNCED UNDERWRITTEN PUBLIC OFFERING OF EQUITY UNITS EXERCISED IN FULL THEIR OVER-ALLOTMENT OPTION.OPTION EXERCISED WAS TO PURCHASE ADDITIONAL 1.45 MILLION PREPAID FORWARD STOCK PURCHASE CONTRACTS TO CREATE 1.45 MILLION EQUITY UNITS.TOTAL NET PROCEEDS TO PG&E CORPORATION (BEFORE ESTIMATED OFFERING EXPENSES) WAS ABOUT $119 MILLION.EXPECTS TO SETTLE ADDITIONAL EQUITY UNITS ISSUANCE ON AUGUST 3.EXPECTS TO REDEEM ABOUT $121 MILLION OF PREVIOUSLY ANNOUNCED PREPAID FORWARD STOCK PURCHASE CONTRACTS ENTERED INTO WITH CERTAIN INVESTORS.EXPECTS TO ISSUE ABOUT $402 MILLION OF SHARES OF STOCK TO SUCH INVESTORS AT A SETTLEMENT PRICE PER SHARE OF $9.50.PG&E EXPECTS TO ISSUE AN ADDITIONAL 748,415 SHARES OF COMMON STOCK TO PG&E FIRE VICTIM TRUST.'}